From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=81ngel=20Ren=C3=A9?=
 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:46:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: signal the parsed stream format with
 V4L2_EVENT_SOURCE_CHANGE
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The stateful decoder interface (dev-decoder.rst, "Initialization") has
the client learn the stream's coded format from V4L2_EVENT_SOURCE_CHANGE
once the header is parsed; s5p-mfc only sent the event for a resolution
change in the middle of a stream. Queue it when SEQ_DONE leaves the
instance in HEAD_PARSED.

Clients that do not subscribe to the event are not affected.

Tested on a Pixel 7 (gs201, MFC v15.6) with the rest of this series: a
small V4L2 stateful test client that waits for the event, FFmpeg's
h264_v4l2m2m and GStreamer's v4l2h264dec all decode H.264 bit-exact
against FFmpeg's software decoder. Not tested on any older MFC.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c   | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
index 03e7eac8d..87f76d16c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc.c
@@ -540,10 +540,24 @@ static void s5p_mfc_handle_seq_done(struct s5p_mfc_ctx *ctx,
 		if (FW_HAS_E_MIN_SCRATCH_BUF(dev))
 			ctx->scratch_buf_size = s5p_mfc_hw_call(dev->mfc_ops,
 						get_min_scratch_buf_size, dev);
-		if (ctx->img_width == 0 || ctx->img_height == 0)
+		if (ctx->img_width == 0 || ctx->img_height == 0) {
 			ctx->state = MFCINST_ERROR;
-		else
+		} else {
+			static const struct v4l2_event ev_src_ch = {
+				.type = V4L2_EVENT_SOURCE_CHANGE,
+				.u.src_change.changes =
+					V4L2_EVENT_SRC_CH_RESOLUTION,
+			};
+
 			ctx->state = MFCINST_HEAD_PARSED;
+			/*
+			 * The stateful decoder interface (dev-decoder.rst,
+			 * "Initialization"): the client learns the stream's
+			 * format from this event, not by calling G_FMT on
+			 * CAPTURE in a loop.
+			 */
+			v4l2_event_queue_fh(&ctx->fh, &ev_src_ch);
+		}
 
 		if ((ctx->codec_mode == S5P_MFC_CODEC_H264_DEC ||
 			ctx->codec_mode == S5P_MFC_CODEC_H264_MVC_DEC) &&
